    "durationMs": 184154,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified — 35/35 endpoint checks passed, plus a restart test confirming persistence.\n\n**What I built:**\n- **Endpoints**: `POST /links` (201, auto/custom codes), `GET /links` (ascending by creation, `{\"items\", \"total\"}`), `GET /links/{code}`, and `GET /r/{code}` (302 + atomic `UPDATE clicks = clicks + 1`). Errors are JSON `{\"error\": ...}` with 409 for duplicate codes, 404 for unknown codes, and 422 for malformed JSON, missing/invalid urls (scheme+host enforced via `java.net.URI`), and invalid codes (`^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$`).\n- **Persistence**: Spring Data JPA entity mapped to a `links` table created by a Flyway migration (`V1__init.sql`); Hibernate runs in `validate` mode so the schema stays migration-managed. Generated codes come from `SecureRandom` with uniqueness retries.\n- **Config**: An `EnvironmentPostProcessor` converts `DATABASE_URL` (`postgresql://bench:...@postgres:5432/bench`) into JDBC properties at boot — no hard-coded credentials — and the server binds `0.0.0.0:8000`.\n- **start.sh**: `sh start.sh` execs the prebuilt jar in the foreground; Flyway applies pending migrations during startup before Tomcat begins serving (deps were installed during the build, with a rebuild fallback only if the jar is missing). The README documents all of this.\n\nI verified against the live Postgres 16 instance: created/auto-generated codes, duplicate 409s, all 422 validation paths, redirect Location headers with exact one-time click increments, ascending listing with totals, and data surviving a full server restart. My test rows were truncated afterward, so the database is clean for the automated suite."
  }
